      "critic": {
        "decision": "accept",
        "reason": "Accept. (1) Semantics: the multiply-based qh scatter is bit-exact with the baseline. Multiplier 0x02040810 has set bits {4,11,18,25}; for a 4-bit operand the partial products occupy disjoint bit sets (b0->{4,11,18,25}, b1->{5,12,19,26}, b2->{6,13,20,27}, b3->{7,14,21,28}), so no carries, and masking with 0x10101010 yields exactly bit4=b0, bit12=b1, bit20=b2, bit28=b3 \u2014 identical to the baseline vi0 mapping (qh bits 0,1,2,3 -> 4,12,20,28) and, via (vh>>16)&0x0F, the vi1 mapping (bits 16..19 -> 4,12,20,28). Signed-shift sign-fill only touches vh bits >= 20 (shift <= 12 since iqs+i <= 3) while all consumed bits are <= 19; multiply operands are small positives (max product 0x1E43C8F0), no overflow. The hoisted qh load plus per-iteration shift inside the impl is algebraically identical to the removed vh[i] computation. (2) Containment: vec_dot_q5_0_q8_1_impl has no caller outside vec_dot_q5_0_q8_1 (the MMQ Q5_0 path merges qh at tile load and uses vec_dot_q8_0_q8_1_impl), so the signature change is contained within declared symbols; the 1139-case MUL_MAT suite gates any residual risk. (3) Authority: files/symbols are inside cuda-vecdotq-v1; change_class arithmetic matches eligible hypothesis akh-v2-q5-type-specific-dequant; no launch-geometry or wave-count change, so no DNR fingerprint applies (dnr-q5-four-wave is launch_geometry). (4) Dispatch: the three expected_dispatch rows exactly match the hypothesis anchors (grids 57344/8192/311296, wg128, lds1024, calls 6063/4644/3096); the 129-call false/true tail is correctly omitted per the explicit anchor exclusion, and the patch changes no launch geometry so signatures are stable. (5) Plausibility: caveat that v_mul_lo_u32 is quarter-rate on CDNA2, so the gain is smaller than naive op counting suggests (~7 effective cycles vs ~12 full-rate ops per half-word), but reduced instruction count and dropped vh[] register pressure make a positive exact type-6 delta plausible; the declared falsifier (exact kernel duration under correctness-preserving replay, then graphs-on whole-model direction) properly decides the outcome. Load-mode recommendation (cold_serialized under the fallback-only admission profile) is consistent with policy."
      },
